---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../layouts/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Shri Govardhan Goshala collects when you donate, why, and how long it is kept."
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy"
    lede="What we ask for, why we ask, and what we do not collect." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--tight prose legal">
      <p class="legal__meta">Last updated 11 August 2026</p>

      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you donate we ask for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Name, phone and email</strong> — to acknowledge your donation and reach you about it</li>
        <li><strong>The amount and which cause</strong> you chose</li>
        <li><strong>A reference number</strong> we generate for your payment</li>
        <li><strong>Your UPI transaction ID</strong>, if you give it on the confirmation step</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Only if you ask for an 80G receipt, we additionally ask for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>PAN</strong> (or Aadhaar, if you have no PAN) — required on the statement of donations we file</li>
        <li><strong>Postal address</strong> — required on the certificate</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="callout">
        If you do not want a receipt, we do not ask for any identity document
        at all. The previous version of this site required an Aadhaar number
        from every donor; that is no longer the case.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we never collect</h2>
      <p>
        We never ask for and never store card numbers, CVV, UPI PIN, bank
        passwords or OTP. Payment happens entirely inside your own UPI app —
        the money moves between your bank and ours, not through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How it is used</h2>
      <p>
        Your details are used to acknowledge your donation, to match your
        payment against our bank statement, to issue a receipt if you asked for
        one, and to meet our reporting obligations under the Income Tax Act.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell, rent or trade your information, and we do not use it
        for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Who else sees it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> — donation records are held in Google Sheets and email is sent through Gmail</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts the site and passes your submission on to us</li>
        <li><strong>The Income Tax Department</strong> — where a donation is reported for 80G</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Nobody else. Your details are not shared with other charities or any commercial party.</p>

      <h2>5. Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people use.
        It records pages viewed and broad location, not your name or your
        donation details.
      </p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Donation records are kept as long as accounting and tax law requires —
        in practice at least eight years for anything reported under 80G.
        Enquiries not resulting in a donation are cleared periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> to
        ask what we hold about you, to correct it, or to ask us to delete it. We
        cannot delete records we are legally required to retain, and we will say
        so if that applies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--t-lg); }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.75; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .legal__meta {
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-block-end: var(--s-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .legal .callout {
    background: var(--ok-bg);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ok);
    padding: var(--s-4);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
